WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.000
Hey, 42 here.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.440
In 1878 Charles Darwin's cousin,

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:08.790
explorer, inventor, and polymath Sir Francis Galton

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.670
Discovered a new technique to combine

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.660
portraits to create a composite image,

00:00:15.080 --> 00:00:17.460
an average face.

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:22.200
What he discovered was that whenever you average people's faces to create a new face,

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.660
the resulting composite face is always

00:00:25.660 --> 00:00:26.830
beautiful.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:31.709
He thus concluded that as humans we find averages beautiful.

00:00:31.709 --> 00:00:35.800
We dislike extremes, anomalies and oddities.

00:00:36.140 --> 00:00:43.560
Sir Francis Galton deduced that facial symmetry, as well as averageness, both contribute to beauty.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:47.800
Around the same time that Sir Francis Galton published his research

00:00:47.800 --> 00:00:56.040
a Polish businessman by the name of Maximilian Faktorowicz took immense interest in what Galton had to say about beauty.

00:00:56.680 --> 00:01:00.959
Galton's findings inspired Maximilian to create a strange device

00:01:01.149 --> 00:01:08.759
which he called the Beauty Micrometer. Its purpose was to measure a woman's face and check for

00:01:09.240 --> 00:01:15.740
averageness and symmetry. It was able to pick up on minor structural flaws that were barely

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.020
noticeable to the human eye.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:25.420
Women flocked in their droves, mostly from the film industry, to try out Maximilian's new device.

00:01:25.560 --> 00:01:32.600
Conveniently, he also happened to produce and sell a range of beauty-enhancing products to fix the so-called

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:37.320
imperfections that the beauty micrometer picked up on.

00:01:37.460 --> 00:01:39.460
He named these products

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:41.400
makeup.

00:01:41.409 --> 00:01:45.449
So successful was his range of makeup, that he started a company

00:01:46.210 --> 00:01:48.210
named after himself.

00:01:49.030 --> 00:01:51.030
Maximilian Faktorowicz

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:53.100
Max Factor

00:01:53.180 --> 00:01:58.380
Which as you all know, would become one of the largest makeup brands in the world.

00:01:59.140 --> 00:02:06.240
But this raises a poignant question – why do we find symmetry and averageness to be beautiful?

00:02:06.240 --> 00:02:11.080
Why aren't quirky, odd, and disfigured faces

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:12.500
considered beautiful,

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.500
by most people?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:18.000
Researchers have longed for, that the reason for this is that imperfect,

00:02:18.040 --> 00:02:20.860
asymmetrical faces can indicate

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:28.200
That potential mates have an ailment or a disease and so the laws of sexual selection dictate that we are

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.860
predisposed to choose not to mate with such people because they may produce

00:02:33.480 --> 00:02:35.740
unfavorable offspring.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:42.250
Although this is not a very nice theory, it does make sense after all, it's true that various diseases

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:46.029
we can have as children do leave permanent scars and

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:50.529
physical disfigurement on your face and body in some cases.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.540
Albeit less so today with modern medicine.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:03:00.000
But, if this were true wouldn't so-called "ugliness" and "physical imperfections"

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.620
have died out long ago through sexual selection?

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:06.180
Kind of like a natural eugenics?

00:03:06.640 --> 00:03:13.500
Well, there must be more to this beauty thing than wanting to avoid a disease and genetic disorders.

00:03:13.720 --> 00:03:19.240
Also, today with modern medicine illnesses we have as children such as chickenpox,

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:26.100
Rarely leave any permanent physical marks and our faces, as they would have done so in our hunter-gatherer days.

00:03:26.780 --> 00:03:33.790
The answer to why we find symmetrical faces so beautiful could in fact be so simple.

00:03:34.130 --> 00:03:36.130
It's almost beautiful.

00:03:36.560 --> 00:03:43.080
Some scientists think it's simply because humans find beauty in all things symmetrical in nature.

00:03:43.840 --> 00:03:46.480
Symmetry represents order, calmness,

00:03:46.980 --> 00:03:54.220
and certainty. It is the opposite of chaos, so seeing symmetry whether it's in nature or a

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:59.110
Significant other's face makes us feel calm and content.

00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:01.670
Be it the wings of a butterfly,

00:04:02.120 --> 00:04:09.620
The orderly leaves of a plant, all the gentle ripples in a pond all these sights bring us peace.

00:04:09.840 --> 00:04:14.300
The same chemical reactions that caused these feelings of content,

00:04:14.610 --> 00:04:18.230
could also be triggered by the symmetry in a person's face.

